summary:
- topic: Kaler Elementary Modified Schedule
  text: The board approved a modified end-of-year schedule for Kaler Elementary to
    accommodate the school's closure and move. The plan includes an early release
    on June 15th and a day off on June 16th, with the administration noting that over
    90% of Kaler teachers supported the change.
- topic: Childcare for Kaler Families
  text: A significant portion of the discussion focused on providing free, district-funded
    childcare for Kaler families impacted by the schedule change. The administration
    reported on survey results and committed to working with the city's recreation
    program and exploring other community partners to meet the need.
- topic: Interim Superintendent Appointment
  text: The board appointed Andy Wallace as interim superintendent for two weeks in
    July to cover a gap between the outgoing and incoming superintendents. Mr. Wallace
    will receive four vacation days as compensation, as he declined a salary for the
    short-term role.
- topic: Recognition for Assistant Superintendent
  text: The board unanimously approved a one-time $12,000 contribution to Assistant
    Superintendent Jo Prince's retirement plan. Board members praised her for taking
    on extensive responsibilities related to the budget process and school reconfiguration
    during a difficult year.
- topic: Resignation of Director of Operations and Security
  text: The superintendent announced the resignation of Mike Nalli, Director of Operations
    and Security. Board members expressed regret, calling it a significant loss and
    praising his contributions to improving district safety and his reliability in
    handling urgent situations.
- topic: Kaler Family Transition Efforts
  text: The administration reported positive community-building efforts, with PTA
    leaders from all elementary schools collaborating to plan welcoming events for
    Kaler families. Successful open houses were also held at the receiving schools
    to help ease the transition.
